:"Ceramides are a family of waxy lipid molecules that, alongside cholesterol and free fatty acids, form the extracellular mortar of the stratum corneum. They make up roughly 50% of the skin's lipid content by mass."}]}],["$","$L3","1",{"delay":0.03,"children":["$","p",null,{"className":"font-serif text-lg md:text-xl leading-[1.6] text-foreground/90 mb-6","children":"Their role is structural. Ceramides organise themselves into lamellar bilayers that hold corneocytes in place and seal in water. When ceramide levels drop — through ageing, over-cleansing, harsh actives or winter climate — that lamellar structure weakens and water escapes."}]}],["$","$L3","2",{"delay":0.06,"children":["$","p",null,{"className":"font-serif text-lg md:text-xl leading-[1.6] text-foreground/90 mb-6","children":"Not all ceramide products are equal. The skin's natural ratio of ceramides : cholesterol : free fatty acids is approximately 3 : 1 : 1. Formulations that mirror this ratio replenish the barrier more effectively than formulations that simply add ceramides in isolation."}]}],["$","$L3","3",{"delay":0.09,"children":["$","p",null,{"className":"font-serif text-lg md:text-xl leading-[1.6] text-foreground/90 mb-6","children":"AUREL's Ceramide Recovery Cream and Overnight Barrier Mask are both formulated around the 3:1:1 ratio. The result is a barrier that holds water better and visibly recovers faster from stress."}]}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-border","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs text-muted-foreground font-mono uppercase tracking-wider","children":"AUREL is a fictional concept brand. Articles are educational demonstration content and do not constitute medical advice."}]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"bg-bone-deep py-16 md:py-24","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container-aurel","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-eyebrow text-muted-foreground mb-8","children":"Mentioned in this article"}],"$L5"]}]}],"$L6"]}]],["$L7"]